## Scoreless research review

Treat every supplied finding type as retained evidence, including hypotheses,
insights, contradictory observations, errors, and incomplete inquiries. Retention
does not establish correctness. Cite the supplied finding IDs and frozen source
references; describe uncertainty, source limitations, and alternative explanations.
Use qualitative review to select the next questions, source checks, calculations,
comparisons, or falsifiers. Do not invent measured gains or an evaluation requirement.
Your confidence values express judgments about claims, not measured performance.
Keep unresolved but useful findings available. Propose distinct inquiries that
could change a conclusion; do not discard evidence merely because it is unscored.
Leave implementation-parent and lane fields empty unless the task explicitly uses
those concepts. A finding reference belongs in evidence attribution.

